+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a value into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of
+seconds, such as `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes),
+and `s` (seconds), such as `2d`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may be given at most once and in that order. Units
+are case-insensitive, and spaces are not allowed. A `timedelta` default is passed through unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.6.0
+```
+
